From a16afcf592307d606059cb67656e15a81fb073dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:29:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] revert(ux): keep issue mutations JSON-by-default (UX4a needs
 a design decision)

The mutation human-render conflicted with a deliberate, tested contract: forge
create/claim/close return a machine-parseable JSON envelope by default so scripts and
pipes work without --json (test/commands/issue-human-output.test.js, non-interactive-
banner-stderr.test.js). Making writes human-first is a breaking output-contract change,
so it needs an explicit call (leave-JSON / human-always / TTY-aware). Reverting the
render change here; the other four journey-audit fixes (claim guard, prime/orient
placeholder, filesystem wording, DEP0190) stand. Tracked as 60e196f4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md                 |  2 +-
 lib/commands/_issue.js       |  6 +-----
 lib/issue-render.js          | 37 +-----------------------------------
 test/commands/_issue.test.js |  7 ++-----
 test/issue-render.test.js    | 36 -----------------------------------
 5 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b7da4292..c22796fe 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ First public release. The default issue backend changed from Beads to the built-
 ### Fixed
 
 - **The core workflow is now reachable out of the box after `forge init` / `forge setup`.** Previously, lefthook's own postinstall dropped a fully-commented stub `lefthook.yml` that blocked Forge from writing a real config, so `forge plan` / `dev` / `ship` all dead-ended on `HOOKS_NOT_ACTIVE: missing required hooks: pre-commit, pre-push`. Forge now writes a minimal user-facing lefthook config wiring the self-contained TDD gate (`.forge/hooks/check-tdd.js`) on pre-commit and the project's own tests on pre-push — referencing only files a user project actually has (never Forge's repo-internal `scripts/`) — and overwrites the disposable stub while never clobbering a real config. (#334)
-- End-to-end new-user UX polish (all surfaced by a fresh-project journey audit): `forge claim`/`show`/etc. with no id now return a clean "Missing required argument <id>" and a non-zero exit instead of fabricating a random UUID and quarantining it; `forge create`/`claim`/`close` and the other writes print a concise human confirmation (`✓ Created <id>`) instead of dumping the raw contract JSON (still available via `--json`/`FORGE_JSON=1`); `forge prime`/`orient` no longer show internal "D21 placeholder" text; the kernel filesystem note dropped its alarming "database corruption" wording on the fail-open path; and `forge init` no longer emits a Node `DEP0190` deprecation warning. (#334)
+- End-to-end new-user UX polish (all surfaced by a fresh-project journey audit): `forge claim`/`show`/etc. with no id now return a clean "Missing required argument <id>" and a non-zero exit instead of fabricating a random UUID and quarantining it; `forge prime`/`orient` no longer show internal "D21 placeholder" text; the kernel filesystem note dropped its alarming "database corruption" wording on the fail-open path; and `forge init` no longer emits a Node `DEP0190` deprecation warning. (#334)
 - `forge export` now actually projects Kernel issues to git-tracked JSONL. The command dispatcher injects a Kernel broker for `export`, and Kernel mutations enqueue the projection-outbox marker under the `jsonl` target the export consumer drains — so the Kernel git-persistence/portability loop works end to end. (#270)
 - First-run hint from `forge status` pointed at a nonexistent docs topic (`forge docs workflow`); it now points at `forge docs setup`. (#334)
 - Removed stale "Beads" wording from live `forge --help` output — the `board` and `test` command descriptions now reference the kernel. (#334)
